# Cursor Rules — STRICT MODE (Generic)
# Goal: Do exactly what I ask. No unsolicited edits, refactors, or formatting changes.

[PRINCIPLES]
- Obey explicit commands only. If not explicitly requested, DO NOTHING.
- Keep diffs minimal and localized to the command. Do not touch unrelated files/lines.
- Preserve existing style, naming, imports, comments, and ordering unless I say otherwise.
- No "improvements," "optimizations," or "cleanups" unless explicitly requested.
- Never auto-fix lint/format; only format the exact code you were asked to add/modify.

[ALLOWED WITHOUT FURTHER CONFIRMATION]
- Create/modify exactly the files, functions, or lines I name.
- Add imports strictly required for the code I asked you to add.
- Resolve compiler/runtime errors that are direct consequences of the requested change (only minimal fix).

[REQUIRE EXPLICIT COMMAND]
- Renames (files, symbols, routes, env keys).
- Refactors (split/merge files, change architecture, convert syntax/framework versions).
- Dependency changes (package.json/pubspec/podfile/gradle) and build config.
- Lint/format across files, comment reflow, or reordering code blocks.
- Deleting any code or files.

[PROHIBITED]
- Editing unrelated files or test snapshots.
- Changing environment variables or endpoints.
- Introducing new patterns (e.g., hooks, services, DI, state libraries) unless told.
- Swapping libraries or upgrading dependencies.
- Rewriting commit history.

[DIFF QUALITY]
- Smallest possible change-set. No churn.
- Keep line endings/whitespace as-is. Avoid rewrapping strings.
- Maintain current error handling and logging style.

[MESSAGING]
- When I issue a command, respond with: (1) a bullet list of intended edits, (2) the diff preview.
- If something blocks the exact command (e.g., missing symbol), propose ONE minimal resolution.

[TESTS]
- Only add or update tests when explicitly requested, or when the change breaks existing tests; then fix only the failing tests related to the change.

[FILE OPERATIONS]
- New files: create only when I name them. Place in the exact path I specify.
- Existing files: update only the sections I point to by line/function/marker comments.

[SECURITY & SECRETS]
- Never add, print, or log secrets/keys/tokens.
- Do not modify auth flows, RBAC, or network endpoints unless the command says so.

[COMMIT / PR]
- Single focused commit per command, title: "<scope>: <short action>". No decorative emojis.
- PR title mirrors commit; description lists the exact commands executed.

[RECOVERY]
- If the instruction is ambiguous or unsafe, STOP and ask a single clarifying question.